  1268	      // defensively if a runtime ever does. Any other error (a broken context) leaves the entry for
  1269	      // synchronize_and_release_all, which re-queries it and reports and leaks it if the device cannot synchronize.
  1270	      // P1T-FIX4 (sweep): that other error's slot entry is consumed here (62c8d9f left it, so the next, unrelated
  1271	      // launch check reported it as its own); the entry itself still carries the failure to synchronize().
