  1273	      // stays queued, but a queued entry does not remember the error: synchronize() re-queries it, and if the query now
  1274	      // succeeds the entry is released and synchronize() returns success, so the failure was consumed and never
  1275	      // reported (review probe query_error_cpu.py / query_error_single_gpu.py; FIX4 sweep rows 47 and 50). Now a
  1276	      // non-NotReady failure is RECORDED first (counted in event_query_failures and noted as a failure where nothing
  1277	      // can raise: the drain is noexcept and runs at the start of an unrelated call), and only then is the slot entry
  1278	      // consumed; the next synchronize() raises it exactly once (FIX4's deferred-error routing, cleared once its message
  1279	      // exists). Completion and release stay as before: the entry is left for synchronize(), which re-queries it and
  1280	      // releases on a successful query, or leaks it with no completion proof. NotReady is not recorded: CUDA 12.6
  1281	      // documents it as "not considered an error" (Programming Guide 3.2.12) and it is not an error of the query.
  1282	      // Prior art: NVIDIA CUDA 12.6 cudaEventQuery / cudaGetLastError contracts (a returned error vs the per-thread slot);
