### Prior art

V7-01 uses CPython 3.12’s documented [float overflow](https://docs.python.org/3.12/library/functions.html#float) and [finalization/GIL rules](https://docs.python.org/3.12/c-api/init.html), DLPack ownership, and C++17 `noexcept` semantics. The finite-callback staging comes from REV5/6; this review adds the diagnostic-conversion bypass scenario. V7-02 uses the distinct [CUDA event-query contract](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/archive/12.6.0/cuda-runtime-api/group__CUDART__EVENT.html); its proposed failure-kind tag is ordinary error attribution, with no specific prior art known to me.

